course: dictionary
lesson: 7489
title: Possibly: maybe, or not at all
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word possibly is a small clue about how sure someone is. Look at the words around it to find out whether the writer is doubtful, or is being polite. «It will swallow Mercury and Venus and possibly the Earth» means the writer is not certain about the Earth.
explain: Check the words next to possibly. With can or could, it means in any way possible: «I'll come as soon as I possibly can» means as soon as I am able. With can't, it means impossible: «a cake can't possibly make me larger» means a cake cannot make you bigger at all.
explain: Possibly also appears in polite questions, such as «Could you possibly help me?» Here it makes the request gentler. A quick test: swap in perhaps or maybe. If the sentence still makes sense, possibly means the same thing.
fact: Possibly means perhaps or maybe, when something could be true but you are not sure.
fact: With can or could, possibly means in any way possible, as in «as much breakfast as I can possibly eat».
fact: With can't, possibly means impossible, as in «I can't possibly eat all that».
fact: In polite talk, «Could you possibly help me?» is a very polite way to ask for help.
fact: Probably is a stronger word than possibly, because it means something is more likely to happen.
exercise: In «possibly the Earth», what does possibly mean? | *Perhaps, but not certain | Very quickly | Never at all | Definitely, with no doubt at all
exercise: Alice says, «a cake can't possibly make me larger». What does can't possibly mean? | It might be true | It is very likely | *It is impossible | It is very kind
exercise: «I'll come as soon as I possibly can.» What does possibly mean here? | Never, not at all | *In any way possible, meaning as soon as I am able | Very loudly | In any way possible
test: «Could you possibly help me?» Why does the speaker use possibly? | To show they are certain | *To make the request polite | To say that help is impossible | To make the request louder
test: The Footman says «no one could possibly hear you». What does this suggest? | *Nobody at all could hear you | Someone might hear you, perhaps | Everyone heard you clearly | Hearing is very easy
exam: Which word shows a stronger sign that something is likely than possibly? | *Probably | Barely | Drooped | Curt
